Added transpose.js to the chat.
To implement the `transpose` function according to the instructions, I will 
replace the placeholder implementation in `transpose.js`.



The algorithm will:

1. Split the input string into lines.

2. Determine the maximum line length to know how many rows the transposed output
will have.

3. Iterate through each column index (which becomes the row index in the 
output).

4. For each output row, iterate through the original lines (columns).

5. Collect characters, handling padding:

   - If a character exists at the current position in the original line, add it.

   - If not, check if any subsequent original line has a character at this 
column index. If so, pad with a space (left padding). If not, stop adding to 
this output row (no right padding).

6. Join the collected characters for each output row and join all output rows 
with newlines.



transpose.js

