To implement the number-to-English conversion as requested, I will replace the contents of `lib.rs` with a complete implementation. This implementation handles numbers from 0 up to the maximum `u64` value (approx 18 quintillion), breaking them down into chunks of thousands and converting each chunk to English words, then appending the appropriate scale (thousand, million, billion, trillion, quadrillion, quintillion).

Here is the plan:
1.  Define helper arrays for small numbers (0-19) and tens (20-90).
2.  Implement a helper function `encode_chunk` to convert numbers 0-999 into English.
3.  Implement the main `encode` function to:
    *   Handle 0 specifically.
    *   Iterate through the number in chunks of 1000 (using division and modulo).
    *   Convert each chunk and append the corresponding scale word.
    *   Join the parts with spaces.

lib.rs
```rust
pub fn encode(n: u64) -> String {
    if n == 0 {
        return "zero".to_string();
    }

    let small_numbers = [
        "zero", "one", "two", "three", "four", "five", "six", "seven", "eight", "nine",
        "ten", "eleven", "twelve", "thirteen", "fourteen", "fifteen", "sixteen", "seventeen",
        "eighteen", "nineteen",
    ];

    let tens = [
        "", "", "twenty", "thirty", "forty", "fifty", "sixty", "seventy", "eighty", "ninety",
    ];

    let scales = ["", " thousand", " million", " billion", " trillion", " quadrillion", " quintillion"];

    fn encode_chunk(n: u64, small_numbers: &[&str], tens: &[&str]) -> String {
        let mut parts = Vec::new();
        if n >= 100 {
            parts.push(small_numbers[(n / 100) as usize]);
            parts.push(" hundred");
        }
        let remainder = n % 100;
        if remainder >= 20 {
            parts.push(tens[(remainder / 10) as usize]);
            if remainder % 10 > 0 {
                parts.push(&small_numbers[(remainder % 10) as usize]);
            }
        } else if remainder > 0 {
            parts.push(small_numbers[remainder as usize]);
        }
        parts.join("")
    }

    let mut parts = Vec::new();
    let mut scale_idx = 0;
    let mut remaining = n;

    while remaining > 0 {
        let chunk = remaining % 1000;
        remaining /= 1000;

        if chunk > 0 {
            let chunk_str = encode_chunk(chunk, &small_numbers, &tens);
            let scale = scales[scale_idx];
            parts.push(format!("{}{}", chunk_str, scale));
        }
        scale_idx += 1;
    }

    parts.reverse();
    parts.join(" ")
}
```
